    "created_at": "2020-05-04T12:07:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-04T12:10:51Z",
    "body": "> Indeed this is possible, but it would require us to either modularize the config or change how we support different shells, since bash doesn't support anything like RPROMPT.\r\n\r\nif there would be an `rprompt` module, it could be disabled by default and users of zsh/fish could enable it on demand.\r\n\r\nEdit: Just looked at the init scripts and I think its even simpler. The bash init script just dont need to call anything regarding rprompt.",
